  "result": "I wrote the rule and witnesses for LVMC_11_52_136 (\"No person shall park a vehicle in an access aisle\"), and the gate returned **OK** on its first run, using 1 of the 6 runs.\n\n**Rule** (`LVMC_11_52_136.lean`)\n- **Who it applies to:** the subject must be a vehicle under the `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle` aggregate.\n- **When it applies:** the subject occupies some parking-space region whose designation is `access_aisle`.\n- **The duty:** in every access aisle the subject occupies, it must not be parked. \"Parked\" uses `drv.motion.parked` with `p.halt_speed_tolerance` and `p.parking_min_duration`. The duty repeats the full aisle selection from the applicability, so both formulas refer to the same region.\n- I chose nothing the node left open, so the rule has no narrowings of its own.\n\n**Witnesses**\nScenes are 10 s apart, and each witness only judges instants from 200 s on. That keeps the 180 s parking look-back inside the trace.\n\n| Witness | Scene | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `forbid` | car at rest in the access aisle for 300 s | violated |\n| `permit` | car drives up, halts in the aisle from 200 s to 260 s, drives off | compliant |\n| `idle` | car parked 300 s in a general bay | not applicable |\n| `blind` | car at rest in the disabled bay next to the aisle, occupancy masked | unknown |\n| `branch_1` (added) | a pedestrian stands in the aisle | not applicable |\n\nI added `branch_1` so that some witness tests the vehicle-class check.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
